&lt;hr /&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="14653580" author="githubbot" created="Tue, 4 Aug 2015 12:56:58 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Github user tzolov commented on the pull request:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;    &lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/apache/incubator-zeppelin/pull/180#issuecomment-127595901&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;https://github.com/apache/incubator-zeppelin/pull/180#issuecomment-127595901&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;    Note that if the Interpreter has not not been loaded yet the response for the first Ctrl+. will be delayed.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="14653914" author="tzolov" created="Tue, 4 Aug 2015 16:26:10 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;I drew this sequence diagram to help me understand how the auto-completion event flow works. &lt;br/&gt;
It illustrates the completion path, but most parts of it are generic and common for all Zeppelin websocket operations.  &lt;/p&gt;</comment>
